description:
Implement a `deepClone` function that creates a deep copy of an object or array. The clone must not share any references with the original. Handle nested objects, arrays, `null`, and primitives.

**Example:**
```js
const obj = { a: 1, b: { c: 2 } };
const clone = deepClone(obj);
clone.b.c = 99;
console.log(obj.b.c) // 2 — original unchanged
```

